  "name": "24 HR URINARY URIC ACID",
  "code": "1005",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>The 24-hour urinary uric acid test measures the amount of uric acid excreted in urine over a full day. Its interpretation helps assess uric acid metabolism, kidney function, and risk for conditions like gout or kidney stones.I</p>\n<p>Higher-than-normal levels of uric acid in the urine often indicate gout or kidney stones. Other causes include:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>A diet high in foods containing purines.</li>\n<li>Obesity.</li>\n<li>Liver disease.</li>\n<li>Kidney disease.</li>\n<li>Bone marrow disorders, such as leukemia.</li>\n<li>Metastatic cancer, or cancer that has spread to other parts of the body.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Lower-than-normal levels of uric acid in the urine. This may indicate:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Lead poisoning.</li>\n<li>Alcoholism.</li>\n<li>A diet low in purines.</li>\n</ul>",
